\title{Univariate and Multilinear Polynomials}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    Two representations of the same data, supporting different arguments. The univariate world pairs with low-degree testing; the multilinear world pairs with [sumcheck](dhsorens-002Q). Knowing which one a protocol lives in explains most of its shape.
}

\p{
    To work through:
    \ul{
        \li{The multilinear extension of a function on the Boolean hypercube; uniqueness; the equality polynomial and its role.}
        \li{Degree versus number of variables as the size parameter, and what each buys.}
        \li{Why FRI wants univariate and Basefold, HyperPlonk, and Binius want multilinear.}
        \li{How [WHIR](dhsorens-003C) unifies the two, and what the translation costs.}
        \li{Computable representations — dense, sparse, coefficient, evaluation form — and which operations each makes cheap. This is [CompPoly](dhsorens-0041)'s design problem.}
    }
}
